  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:3f34205e2489c1607f886fce5e38ef18af0e8560deacbeb07802793cab00acdb",
      "text": "Using $createObjectId in an update does not remove the immutability of an existing stored _id. Generate an ordinary identifier field when updating stored documents; the official example that supplies a new _id operates on a view projection. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/document/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:275b266b6f06ac4e355b2f0220e96f9ccb041848aeaf512c839b05ae821c0d3f",
        "ev:fc83324f546d1125d5e9346d14e9a7b0b8195d971525e64d8dcc45750628790d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3d8a4caa2e5b22716ecf8620a7d7952de63cf730d5a38122360679c0a768e526",
      "text": "A first-hand experiment using MongoDB 8.3.11 reports that $createObjectId fails when FCV is 8.2 and succeeds after FCV is set to 8.3. Treat this as a reported compatibility observation, pending independent runtime reproduction. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-11)",
      "source_url": "https://dev.to/alexgeorgiev17/mongodb-83s-arrayindexas-cuts-a-map-with-index-workarounds-overhead-by-up-to-31-409p",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:78ac4cda16ea685203bc2f9d3abeeb9b1769701e35fde93d3c284f02f4d79bdb",
        "ev:86e167ea000291b0f6d5b400e89f55b4ed46b161a196e24b88d334340ca71068"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d5b5a6ef018927df8cf4b84812d0a785b1d0808957505fdb2e64752df52b01e6",
      "text": "The wire expression is {$createObjectId: {}}. Only an empty object is accepted; other arguments fail with FailedToParse. A published first-hand experiment reproduces rejection of {x: 1}. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://dev.to/alexgeorgiev17/mongodb-83s-arrayindexas-cuts-a-map-with-index-workarounds-overhead-by-up-to-31-409p"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6b1a501eff4f3057a5aaa3808d59ee705c3869d45b70a05f48c127daae396521",
        "ev:f4567673a0642b9296e3d5b5a475d0b757fd912d4428b5f046b93471681cde3a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8f7f3aadb9b6d44988a3b80ae3424e436161cbd183de4a9ff6da5b23b66e9bb7",
      "text": "MongoDB introduced $createObjectId in 8.3 to generate new random ObjectId values within aggregation pipelines and expression-based updates. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/release-notes/8.3/",
        "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-106452"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:689114b05e114a2a58a96326de916bdcf6af4f1dda710ca0fe62a649027993be"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:92694a7a3fca7f6d2b56b2b15fc59559976e632b52980d35d6c22bc613e52665",
      "text": "$createObjectId generates a value without a source-value input; $toObjectId converts an existing value. NoSQLBooster documents this distinction alongside its $.createObjectId() helper. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.nosqlbooster.com/blog/announcing-nosqlbooster-11-1/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0e3bdd5a50eb69875813acd8d6040720efc682b5628c04de2742a1c68cfa9988",
        "ev:6b1a501eff4f3057a5aaa3808d59ee705c3869d45b70a05f48c127daae396521"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6b9575502eae7d905bc2685e4fc9cac2f394c60e9198e23abfe2cb492886bed1",
      "text": "Generation occurs for output documents: the official view example assigns _id: {$createObjectId: {}}, and the C# LINQ example assigns a new NewId for each output document using Mql.CreateObjectId(). (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/csharp/current/aggregation/linq/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:fc83324f546d1125d5e9346d14e9a7b0b8195d971525e64d8dcc45750628790d",
        "ev:ffde1010509014b9a06ed13fe988e0d52ed500cbddc237ef185294817d7c4b1b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bb843791cbc26542a524af2e6595f5a3c8d3422574270872b7568791cad3b945",
      "text": "A supported update pattern is db.items.updateMany({}, [{$set: {generatedId: {$createObjectId: {}}}}]); this combines the documented expression-based-update support with the documented pipeline $set stage. This is a documentation-derived example, not a locally executed test. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/update-documents-with-aggregation-pipeline/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5828ba3084ddaa21ca467017f99fdad1a87f372f354c75a722e5a12a02620340",
        "ev:689114b05e114a2a58a96326de916bdcf6af4f1dda710ca0fe62a649027993be",
        "ev:ea54ffc3338c060ac4a2416005e0771701ebaa21fa7906b8d4136a103a182ef7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3a46e8fbc3ebb524df684c3563c9f74636ffb80b8db0798b0dbbd975642d02b9",
      "text": "In a Stack Overflow exchange, a commenter reported the same ObjectId in all array objects. The answer author acknowledged the issue and updated the answer, whose code uses $function with a JavaScript body returning an ObjectId for each mapped element. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://api.stackexchange.com/2.3/questions/68119736/answers?site=stackoverflow&filter=withbody",
      "also": [
        "https://api.stackexchange.com/2.3/answers/68119895/comments?site=stackoverflow&filter=withbody"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:33d8b89e191854209fbfdfea17a3db84dc930521c30192c3ce136eb81287df0c",
        "ev:fce30c055c5e84da44ec400725f9ead74b3436322b79661b1698ce299de46c68"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:97e03924468d09de04ec410ecde3bb97745ee359f2e0b36b8c9eccfeb8a8952f",
      "text": "NoSQLBooster 11.1 exposes $.createObjectId() as an aggregation expression helper; its release announcement dates this support to September 30, 2026. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-30)",
      "source_url": "https://www.nosqlbooster.com/blog/announcing-nosqlbooster-11-1/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
